{
  "world": 11,
  "name": "the Canyon of Banners",
  "note": "The PvP arena for capture the flag (handlers/ctf.go, entity/ctf.go; claude-notes/ctf-world-20261110.md): Box Canyons, one zone of the disc, where it stands on the disc (Tunaria's cell 10, 10). Its southern canyon system is the field: two fingers of canyon floor pointing north between unclimbable mesas, the Ember Band's to the west and the Dusk Band's in the middle, each a camp and a banner stand deep inside a narrowing mouth, joined at their mouths by a long low valley with a mound in it (the middle field), and two side pockets off it, the south-west run and the south-east lobe, with the speed shrines; a heal spring mid-valley. Built by cmd/worldbuild from the operator's disc; the arena block is read by the server, never written into the file. The decoration is the zone's extras (the homes-edges composer's format: the disc's art copied into the zone and placed as actors of its own): two watchtowers splitting the bases' mouths, each team's guild banners beside its stand behind a low wall, lean-tos, braziers and a catapult at each camp, ruined walls, boulders and a wrecked catapult as staggered cover in the valley, the two sun flags on the mound at its middle, and boulders closing the south run, the field's one way out. A composer without extras builds the zone undecorated, as it is on the disc.",
